// Title: Mount Execution With Hidepid Parameter
// Sigma ID: ec52985a-d024-41e3-8ff6-14169039a0b3
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Joseliyo Sanchez, @Joseliyo_Jstnk
// Date: 2023-01-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, stealth, T1564
// Description: Detects execution of the "mount" command with "hidepid" parameter to make invisible processes to
//   other users from the system
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blogs.blackberry.com/
//   - https://www.cyberciti.biz/faq/linux-hide-processes-from-other-users/
//   - https://twitter.com/Joseliyo_Jstnk/status/1620131033474822144
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_mount_hidepid.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/mount" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "hidepid=2" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -o ")
